rung             live  killed  survived  unreached  equiv  killed/reached     killed/live     wall
R5 refinement       1       1         0          0      0      1/1 = 100%      1/1 = 100%     171s

  live       mutants that change observable behaviour. Equivalent ones are excluded
             from every denominator: no rung can kill them, so counting them would
             understate every rung for a reason that is not about the rung.
  survived   the rung's own inputs DO elicit the difference and it passed anyway.
             A gap in the rung.
  unreached  live, but nothing in this rung's input source elicits the difference.
             A gap in the inputs. F009 is the worked example. For a proof rung the
             input source is the contract: unreached means the verifier reads none
             of the files the mutant edits.
  capped     the corner has no verifier for this rung. Not a measurement; shown
             per mutant and per corner, in no denominator.
  killed/reached  the rung's ORACLE. reached = live - unreached = killed +
                  survived. Every rate is printed as its own fraction because a
                  percentage travels and its denominator does not: 100% over two
                  reached cells and 100% over eighteen are the same string and not
                  the same claim (F008).
  killed/live     the rung AS CONFIGURED, inputs included.
  n/a             the denominator is zero -- nothing was reached, so there is no
                  rate. Printed rather than shown as 0%, which is the rate of a
                  rung that saw everything and killed nothing.

